    "proof": "For one odd prime q, exactly the two residues 0 and -2 make q divide n(n+2), so E[X_q]=(q-2-2)/q=1-4/q. The Chinese remainder theorem identifies uniform residues modulo W with the product of uniform residues modulo each q, proving independence. In the product P times the S-monomial, coordinates in S occur squared and contribute one; every omitted coordinate contributes its mean. This corrects, rather than solves, the balanced Boolean stress model: local bias creates signal, but proving a positive gap-two prime correlation still requires a scale-growing arithmetic Type-II estimate and control of the omitted-prime tail.",
    "bias_formula": "mu_q=1-4/q; correlation(S)=product_(q notin S)mu_q",
